What about good?

537
00:21:00,942 --> 00:21:02,662
I don't know what "good" means.

538
00:21:02,662 --> 00:21:05,062
But, sir...

539
00:21:05,062 --> 00:21:08,422
You were talking like you're really good at it.

540
00:21:08,422 --> 00:21:11,102
But I don't think you're good at it.

541
00:21:11,102 --> 00:21:11,962
That's right.

542
00:21:11,962 --> 00:21:13,482
You just have to beat Soki.

543
00:21:13,482 --> 00:21:14,562
No, no, no...

544
00:21:14,562 --> 00:21:15,442
Inoue?

545
00:21:15,962 --> 00:21:16,722
My tongue.

546
00:21:16,722 --> 00:21:17,072
Tongue.

547
00:21:17,072 --> 00:21:19,072
It's so stupid.

548
00:21:21,072 --> 00:21:22,072
Then it's no good.

549
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:24,072
That's why you're not good at this game.

550
00:21:24,072 --> 00:21:27,072
Most things taste better if you put them in your mouth.

551
00:21:28,072 --> 00:21:29,072
That's not true.

552
00:21:29,072 --> 00:21:30,072
Well then, here you go...

553
00:21:30,072 --> 00:21:33,072
So all five of us tasted the pineapple at once.

554
00:21:33,072 --> 00:21:35,072
I'm fine with the aroma.

555
00:21:35,072 --> 00:21:37,072
Who is this?

556
00:21:37,072 --> 00:21:38,072
This is Shokichi

557
00:21:38,072 --> 00:21:39,072
It's Shokichi, isn't it?

558
00:21:39,072 --> 00:21:40,072
It's Shokichi, isn't it?

559
00:21:40,072 --> 00:21:41,072
Shokichi

560
00:21:41,072 --> 00:21:42,072
This is Shokichi

561
00:21:42,072 --> 00:21:43,072
What is this?

562
00:21:43,072 --> 00:21:45,072
There are 5 kinds

563
00:21:45,072 --> 00:21:46,072
Vegetables

564
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:48,640
Fruits

565
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,640
Oh!

566
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:52,640
Oh!

567
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:54,640
It's that plum.

568
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:56,640
I keep forgetting with that face.

569
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,640
I said I'd forget.

570
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:00,640
All right, then.

571
00:22:00,640 --> 00:22:02,640
Can the five of you guess what's inside?

572
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:06,640
Let's start with Inoue.

573
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:08,640
Open.

574
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,640
Apples, oranges, carrots...

575
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:12,448
Tomatoes. None.

576
00:22:12,448 --> 00:22:14,448
None?

577
00:22:14,448 --> 00:22:18,448
It's got that rough texture.

578
00:22:18,448 --> 00:22:22,448
I thought apples would be like that in a smoothie.

579
00:22:22,448 --> 00:22:26,448
I thought bananas would be thicker.

580
00:22:26,448 --> 00:22:28,448
Cheerful?

581
00:22:28,448 --> 00:22:29,448
Yes, sir.

582
00:22:29,448 --> 00:22:31,448
What? Banana? Please announce.

583
00:22:31,448 --> 00:22:35,448
The first time I changed the scent, I felt banana.

584
00:22:35,448 --> 00:22:37,448
I only have Inoue and orange in my head.

585
00:22:37,448 --> 00:22:38,448
Oh, no.

586
00:22:38,448 --> 00:22:39,008
Oh, my God.

587
00:22:39,008 --> 00:22:43,008
Let's end with something I thought might be in there.

588
00:22:43,008 --> 00:22:47,008
Banana, apple, kiwi, komatsuna, mango...

589
00:22:47,008 --> 00:22:50,008
If they put komatsuna, I wouldn't know.

590
00:22:50,008 --> 00:22:53,008
I cut a banana on the first shot.

591
00:22:53,008 --> 00:22:54,008
Oh, bananas?

592
00:22:54,008 --> 00:22:57,008
It was so strong, I couldn't tell what else was there.

593
00:22:57,008 --> 00:22:59,008
You wrote "banana" too.

594
00:22:59,008 --> 00:23:02,008
I felt it the first time.

595
00:23:02,008 --> 00:23:03,008
Let's go, Plum.

596
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:04,280
Let's go.

597
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:07,280
Celery, apple, banana, pineapple, peach...

598
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:09,280
Celery... No, but...

599
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:13,280
No one else has celery. Celery is very strong.

600
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:15,280
I'm confident about celery, apple and banana.

601
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:18,280
The aroma is banana.

602
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:24,280
And when I drank it, I tasted the apple, and I thought the celery was in the back.

603
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:26,280
Celery is hidden.

604
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:27,280
Celery?

605
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:30,280
It didn't smell too green, so I'm guessing it's not the only vegetable.

606
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:32,280
Maybe not. I don't know.

607
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:33,696
Okay, let's keep going, Don.

608
00:23:33,696 --> 00:23:36,396
Tomatoes, strawberries, kiwis, grapes, carrots.

609
00:23:36,396 --> 00:23:39,496
Oh, he put tomatoes in.

610
00:23:39,496 --> 00:23:41,496
But they're all different.

611
00:23:41,496 --> 00:23:46,496
For the record, Mr. Himura also participated. His answer.

612
00:23:46,496 --> 00:23:48,496
Yes, Don.

613
00:23:48,496 --> 00:23:51,496
Apples, carrots, strawberries, garlic, onions.

614
00:23:51,496 --> 00:23:53,496
No onions.

615
00:23:53,496 --> 00:23:56,496
It's a little pungent, a little spicy.

616
00:23:56,496 --> 00:23:59,496
Apple, carrot, too. It's confirmed.

617
00:23:59,496 --> 00:24:01,496
There's no banana in this.

618
00:24:01,496 --> 00:24:02,496
Oh, no...

619
00:24:02,816 --> 00:24:10,216
I wonder if any of these answers are correct.

620
00:24:10,216 --> 00:24:17,636
Apple, banana, tomato, celery, ginger...

621
00:24:17,636 --> 00:24:19,756
So...

622
00:24:19,770 --> 00:24:25,170
The number of correct answers is the number of points from Sugawara, so Umezawa has 2 base points for winning.

623
00:24:25,170 --> 00:24:29,430
Endo and Inoue won one base point.

624
00:24:29,430 --> 00:24:31,490
How can you not understand this?

625
00:24:31,570 --> 00:24:32,890
I don't get it at all.

626
00:24:32,890 --> 00:24:34,870
You don't know how to do it, do you?

627
00:24:34,870 --> 00:24:36,030
I didn't understand the ginger.

628
00:24:36,030 --> 00:24:38,010
If you say so, I'll say sure.

629
00:24:38,010 --> 00:24:40,050
It's ginger now!

630
00:24:40,050 --> 00:24:40,690
It's definitely ginger!

631
00:24:40,690 --> 00:24:44,630
That's why it's garlic and onions... in my mind.

632
00:24:44,630 --> 00:24:45,010
Ah...

633
00:24:45,344 --> 00:24:55,304
That's why Iyoki, Himura and Shokichi have such stupid tongues, don't they?

634
